war dead or a political statement. That's the issue at the heart of a row over whether

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.000
footballers should be allowed to wear poppies when England plays Scotland on Armistice Day.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:14.000
It's understood both teams have been banned from having them on their shirts because FIFA

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.000
counts the poppy as a political symbol. Well our sports correspondent Richard Conway is

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:24.650
at Wembley for us. Richard. Simon, when England plays Scotland here at Wembley in ten days

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:30.000
time, there are plans already in place to mark Armistice Day. The last post will be

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.320
before kick-off. Poppies will be displayed on the big screens and members of the Royal

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.320
British Legion will be present. In the days leading up to the game, players will visit

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:43.640
war graves too. But that issue of the poppy being displayed on team shirts, well, that

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:49.050
is still to be resolved. Back in 2011, the Football Association

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:55.020
brokered a deal with FIFA which saw England players display the poppy on an armband.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:18:00.000
Now with the team set to play Scotland on Armistice Day, both sides are lobbying FIFA

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.000
in a bid to display the poppy on their shirts.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:07.280
FIFA's rules forbid what it calls "political imagery",

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.280
a view that many believe should not apply to the poppy.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:15.700
It's about standing up to bigotry, to fascism, to racism,

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.710
to religious hate crimes.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:21.630
At what point do FIFA not recognise that we should be celebrating

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:25.630
sacrifice that stood up against such vile, detestable evil?

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:30.000
In a statement, the FA said, "We are working closely with the Royal

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.320
British Legion once again this year to honour and remember the sacrifices made

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:38.650
by those serving in the armed forces. In recent weeks the FA has led

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:42.430
remembrance discussions with FIFA to allow the England team to show its

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:47.570
support for the poppy appeal during the World Cup qualifier with Scotland. The

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:52.010
Welsh FA are also speaking with FIFA ahead of their game with Serbia on

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:56.620
November 12th. FIFA's view in the past has been that the poppy represented a

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.000
political symbol and therefore would not be allowed to be displayed.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:05.500
on national shirts. But I'm told that view within the governing body has changed under

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:10.720
its new leadership and they may now be more sympathetic to the home association's lobbying.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.000
I think it's another sign that FIFA has gone crazy, I'm afraid. Clearly out of touch with

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:18.240
modern day and modern life. I can't see why they can't understand and recognise the loss

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.760
that led to the popular appeal. So another sign of FIFA's inflexibility.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:25.500
If they want to wear it, they shouldn't be able to wear it. They shouldn't be able to tell them

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.710
That no, you can't wear it.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:30.000
They absolutely should be allowed to, it's a disgrace.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.520
many Premier League and football league clubs already display the poppy on

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:41.490
their shirts in the run-up to and on Remembrance Day but FIFA's rules for

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:46.170
national teams mean they could punish associations if they believe the rules

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:54.130
have been breached so senior level discussions between the FA and FIFA have

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:58.460
continued this morning I'm told Simon but in addition to that the Prime

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.000
Minister's spokesperson has also

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:04.840
WEIGHED IN ON THIS SAYING THE DISCUSSIONS ARE BEING HELD, RECOGNIZING AND MARKING

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:09.800
THAT, BUT SAYING THAT PEOPLE SHOULD BE FREE TO MARK REMEMBRANCE DAY BY WEARING THE

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.180
POPPY IF THEY SO CHOOSE.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:15.860
SO THOSE DISCUSSIONS ARE SET TO CONTINUE THIS AFTERNOON AND POSSIBLY FOR THE REST OF

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.860
THIS WEEK.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.040
BUT I THINK ALL SIDES WILL BE HOPING FOR A SWIFT RESOLUTION.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:23.960
IT COULD BE THAT THE ARMBAND SOLUTION SEEN IN 2011 IS THE MOST LIKELY OUTCOME FOR THIS.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:30.000
BUT WE REMAIN TO SEE IF FIFO WILL AGREE TO THAT AS THEY DID FIVE YEARS AGO.

