It's one of the most iconic buildings in the world Scotland Yard the home of

00:25:51.650 --> 00:25:55.610
London's Metropolitan Police but now the headquarters is moving to a former

00:25:55.610 --> 00:26:00.000
police station half a mile away. The old building the Met's base since 1967

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.220
is said to be outdated and too expensive. The new site will still be called Scotland Yard

00:26:05.220 --> 00:26:10.500
and yes, the unmistakable revolving sign will still be stationed outside. Our Home Affairs

00:26:10.500 --> 00:26:13.220
correspondent Daniel Sanford reports.

00:26:13.220 --> 00:26:18.060
Broadway South West 1, a building in keeping without time, the home of Scotland Yard from

00:26:18.060 --> 00:26:19.070
now on.

00:26:19.070 --> 00:26:24.640
It was 1967 when the Metropolitan Police moved into New Scotland Yard, a time before

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:30.000
emails, before computer mapping. The Cray twins were still at large, the great

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:33.470
train robber Bruce Reynolds still on the run.

00:26:33.470 --> 00:26:38.150
10 years later, in 1977, this was modern crime fighting,

00:26:38.150 --> 00:26:40.800
comparing fingerprints by eye.

00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:42.840
Looking back at the pictures of herself,

00:26:42.840 --> 00:26:44.980
Rosalie Gist remembers it well.

00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:47.860
I think I was about 27 then.

00:26:47.860 --> 00:26:50.860
The excitement of working in the world-famous New Scotland

00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:54.810
Yard, but also the casual sexism of the day.

00:26:54.810 --> 00:26:58.960
We would be asked to do things that men weren't asked to do.

00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:00.000
we would be asked to

00:27:00.410 --> 00:27:04.690
to go out and get presents for the boss's wife

00:27:04.690 --> 00:27:07.050
because they'd forgotten it's their birthday.

00:27:07.050 --> 00:27:10.710
- The bird, the blonde bird came in.

00:27:10.710 --> 00:27:12.710
- The Flying Squad, the Sweeney,

00:27:12.710 --> 00:27:15.450
headquartered in New Scotland Yard for decades,

00:27:15.450 --> 00:27:19.230
is perhaps the most famous group of detectives in Britain.

00:27:19.230 --> 00:27:21.310
- You have that sense of pride and achievement

00:27:21.310 --> 00:27:23.610
that you've actually been selected for the squad.

00:27:23.610 --> 00:27:26.860
- Barry Phillips joined the Met in 1975

00:27:26.860 --> 00:27:30.000
and was a Flying Squad detective for 23 years.

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:35.340
Then, almost all the force's main units had head offices at New Scotland Yard.

00:27:35.340 --> 00:27:42.980
It brought together that cross-fertilisation of intelligence, of ideas, of thinking, of camaraderie

00:27:42.980 --> 00:27:46.880
in maintaining the crime-fighting traditions of Scotland Yard.

00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:53.720
From New Scotland Yard, the force had to cope with the IRA bombing campaign and the 7-7 attacks.

00:27:54.220 --> 00:28:00.000
And although many squads are now elsewhere, the top brass will still be based at a new office

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:01.450
in Westminster.

00:28:01.450 --> 00:28:06.730
This will be the fourth Scotland Yard, and they've all varied in sizes.

00:28:06.730 --> 00:28:11.530
The point is, the commissioner and his or her top officers have to be somewhere near

00:28:11.530 --> 00:28:12.580
Whitehall.

00:28:12.580 --> 00:28:17.640
I mean, that's where they go when something desperate happens, on the 7th of July, as

00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:22.640
on 9/11 I ended up in the Cabinet Office briefing room, Cobra, with the Prime Minister of the

00:28:22.640 --> 00:28:23.640
day.

00:28:23.640 --> 00:28:25.610
That's what the job entails.

00:28:25.610 --> 00:28:30.000
So after nearly 50 years of crime reporters standing outside New Scotland Yard in

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:36.110
